# Fingerprints and enrolment data. A published reference is a published
# forgery kit — and so is a single RAW file: measured on this body, one frame
# is enough to estimate K well enough to plant it invisibly in an image the
# camera never took (docs/adversarial.md). So the frames are covered here too,
# not just the .npz. These never leave the machine.
*.npz
data/references/
data/flats/
data/shoots/
*.CR3
*.CR2
*.NEF
*.ARW
*.dng

# Secrets
.env
.env.local
*.key
keystore/

# Foundry
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
contracts/lib/

# JS / TS
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# The Graph
subgraph/build/
subgraph/generated/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Test frames stay local. Publishing enrolment frames publishes the means to
# reconstruct K for that body -- the fingerprint-copy attack needs nothing
# else -- so committing them would hand anyone the ability to forge images
# that this project would then attribute to that camera.
fingerprint/raw-test-files/
_to_delete/
_to_delete/
subgraph/tests/.bin/
subgraph/matchstick.yaml
subgraph/tests/.latest.json
mcp/dist/
